# =============================================================================
# Simple Finance — example environment configuration (placeholders only).
#
# Development: copy to .env in the repository root (git-ignored).
# Production:  place at /data/.env inside the container's appdata directory
#              (admin-owned, 0600 — see docs/SPEC.md §18.1). The entrypoint
#              sources it deliberately as a trusted, admin-only file
#              (AGENT_APP_BLUEPRINT.md §7).
#
# This repository is PUBLIC: never put real identities or figures in any file
# that could be committed. Real values live only in the private installation.
# =============================================================================

# --- Storage ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development data root (defaults to ./data). The production container always
# uses /data — fixed by the product owner, docs/SPEC.md §18.1.
# DATA_DIR=./data
# DATABASE_PATH=            # defaults to $DATA_DIR/simple-finance.sqlite

# --- Authentication (Cloudflare Access) ----------------------------------------
# Issuer:        https://<your-team>.cloudflareaccess.com
# Audience:      the Access application's AUD tag
# Allowed users: exactly the two household identities (comma-separated)
# The app verifies the Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion header itself via jose and
# fails closed when these are missing in production.
# AUTH_ISSUER=
# AUTH_AUDIENCE=
# AUTH_ALLOWED_EMAILS=alex@example.com,sam@example.com
# Optional override (defaults to $AUTH_ISSUER/cdn-cgi/access/certs):
# AUTH_CERTS_URL=

# --- Development identity (NEVER honoured in production) -----------------------
# When AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=true AND the app is not running in production, every
# request is treated as the identity below (no Cloudflare Access needed —
# for local development and previews only).
# AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=false
# AUTH_DEV_IDENTITY_EMAIL=dev@example.com

# --- Server ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=3000
